---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
import { withBase } from '../lib/urls';

// Remove items from this list as the organization decides them, then update
// the wording below to match. When the list is empty the review notice disappears.
const reviewItems = [
  'How long each kind of record is kept (the periods below are proposals).',
  'Which Supabase data region the database uses (chosen when the project is created).',
  'How quickly the organization commits to answering privacy requests.',
  'Whether petition signer names and ZIP codes are shared with recipients by default.',
  'Whether to set a minimum age for petitions, volunteering and the newsletter.',
];

const toc = [
  { id: 'summary', label: 'Summary' },
  { id: 'what-we-collect', label: 'What we collect and why' },
  { id: 'automatic', label: 'Information collected automatically' },
  { id: 'providers', label: 'Service providers' },
  { id: 'sharing', label: 'When we share information' },
  { id: 'retention', label: 'How long we keep it' },
  { id: 'choices', label: 'Your choices and requests' },
  { id: 'security', label: 'Security' },
  { id: 'children', label: 'Children' },
  { id: 'changes', label: 'Changes and contact' },
];
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Get Involved Van collects, uses and protects information submitted through petitions, volunteer sign-ups, contact messages and the newsletter."
  lead="What we collect through this website, why, who processes it for us, and how to ask us to change or delete it."
  updated="2026-10-21"
  reviewItems={reviewItems}
  toc={toc}
>
  <h2 id="summary">Summary</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We collect only what you type into our forms, plus the minimum technical data needed to block spam.</li>
    <li>We use it to run petitions, coordinate volunteers, answer messages and send the newsletter you asked for.</li>
    <li>We do not sell personal information, and we don’t use advertising trackers, analytics tools or tracking cookies.</li>
    <li>You can unsubscribe at any time and ask us to see, correct or delete what we hold about you.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    {site.name} is an independent, nonpartisan community organization serving {site.location.city}, {site.location.state}. In this policy “we” and “us”
    mean {site.name}.
  </p>

  <h2 id="what-we-collect">What we collect and why</h2>
  <table class="stack-table">
    <thead>
      <tr><th scope="col">When you…</th><th scope="col">We collect</th><th scope="col">We use it to</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Sign a petition</th>
        <td data-label="We collect">Full name, email address, ZIP code (when the petition asks for it), the petition you signed, whether you also asked for the newsletter, and the time you signed.</td>
        <td data-label="We use it to">Record your support, prevent duplicate signatures, and deliver the petition as described on its page.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Sign up to volunteer</th>
        <td data-label="We collect">Full name, email address, phone number (optional), the ways you’d like to help, your availability and any comments.</td>
        <td data-label="We use it to">Contact you about volunteer opportunities that fit.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Send a message</th>
        <td data-label="We collect">Name, email address, subject and message.</td>
        <td data-label="We use it to">Read and reply to your message.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Join the newsletter</th>
        <td data-label="We collect">Email address, where you signed up, and when you confirmed or unsubscribed.</td>
        <td data-label="We use it to">Send the updates you asked for, and honor your unsubscribe request.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">RSVP to an event</th>
        <td data-label="We collect">Full name, email address and the number of people coming.</td>
        <td data-label="We use it to">Plan the event and contact you about changes to it.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    Each form also records which version of its consent statement you agreed to. Newsletter sign-ups use double opt-in: you are not subscribed until
    you click the link in the confirmation email we send.
  </p>
  <p>
    Petition signatures are not identity-verified. We limit each petition to one signature per email address, and we may remove signatures that appear
    automated or fraudulent.
  </p>

  <h2 id="automatic">Information collected automatically</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Spam protection.</strong> Our forms may use Cloudflare Turnstile to tell people apart from automated bots. Turnstile processes technical
      information such as your IP address and browser characteristics under Cloudflare’s own privacy policy.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Rate limiting.</strong> To stop floods of fake submissions, we store a one-way, salted fingerprint (hash) of your IP address with the time
      of each submission. We never store the IP address itself, and these fingerprints are deleted automatically after two days.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Hosting logs.</strong> The companies that host this website and our form service may keep standard server logs (such as IP addresses and
      request times) for security and reliability. Our own code does not log names, email addresses or messages.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>No tracking.</strong> We don’t use analytics, advertising pixels or tracking cookies. Our fonts are hosted on this website, so loading a
      page doesn’t contact a font service. Your browser’s session storage remembers, for the current visit only, that the loading screen has already
      been shown; it contains no personal information.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="providers">Service providers</h2>
  <p>We rely on a small number of companies to run the website. They process information on our behalf and only as needed to provide their service:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>GitHub</strong> hosts the public website (GitHub Pages).</li>
    <li><strong>Supabase</strong> stores form submissions in a database and runs the code that receives them.</li>
    <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> provides Turnstile spam protection on forms.</li>
    <li><strong>Resend</strong> sends our transactional email: newsletter confirmations and notices to our organizers about new messages and volunteer sign-ups.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>These services may store and process information in the United States or other countries where they operate.</p>

  <h2 id="sharing">When we share information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Petition recipients.</strong> Each petition page states exactly what its recipient will receive. By default that is signers’ names and
      ZIP codes. We never give recipients your email address.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Organizers.</strong> Our authorized organizers can see submissions in order to do the work you signed up for.</li>
    <li><strong>The law.</strong> We may disclose information if we are legally required to.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell, rent or trade personal information, and we don’t publish signer names or email addresses on this website.</p>

  <h2 id="retention">How long we keep it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Petition signatures: until the petition is delivered or closed, then up to two years as a record of the campaign.</li>
    <li>Volunteer sign-ups: until you ask us to remove them, or after two years without contact.</li>
    <li>Contact messages: up to two years.</li>
    <li>
      Newsletter: while you are subscribed. After you unsubscribe we keep your email address marked “unsubscribed” only so we don’t contact you again,
      unless you ask us to delete it entirely.
    </li>
    <li>Rate-limiting fingerprints: two days.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="choices">Your choices and requests</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Unsubscribe from the newsletter at any time using the link in any of our emails.</li>
    <li>
      Ask to see, correct or delete the information we hold about you by <a href={withBase('/contact/')}>contacting us</a> with the subject “Privacy
      request”{site.contact.email ? <> or emailing <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a></> : null}. We may need to confirm the request comes from you, for example by replying to the email address
      in question.
    </li>
    <li>We aim to respond to privacy requests within 30 days.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="security">Security</h2>
  <p>
    The website and our form service use encrypted HTTPS connections. Submissions are stored in a database that the public cannot read: access is
    limited to the server code that saves submissions and to organizers who sign in to the database dashboard. No system is perfectly secure, but we
    collect as little as possible to limit the risk.
  </p>

  <h2 id="children">Children</h2>
  <p>
    This website is for a general audience, and we welcome students who want to learn about local civic life. We don’t knowingly collect personal
    information from children under 13. If you believe a child under 13 has sent us information, contact us and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">Changes and contact</h2>
  <p>
    If we change this policy we will update this page and the “last updated” date above. Questions about privacy are welcome through our <a
      href={withBase('/contact/')}>contact page</a
    >.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
